<title>USA: Olin sees better microelectronics demand.</title>
<headline>Olin sees better microelectronics demand.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Olin Corp on Wednesday said it believes demand will improve for its microelectronic materials as the year progresses.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company said its first quarter results were affected by lower demand in several metals markets and weaker microelectronic materials sales due to lower industry demand.</p>
<p>First quarter net income from continuing operations was $41.8 million, or $0.80 a share compared with $50.7 million, or $0.96 a share in 1996.</p>
